# Who must approve a change, per path. The only CODEOWNERS file: GitHub
# reads the first of .github/, the root and docs/, so a second one would be
# silently ignored.
#
# GitHub applies the LAST line that matches a path, so: the fallback first,
# then one line per team, then the paths only catalog admins may
# approve, last, so no team line can override them. Owners must be
# users or teams with write access to this repository; an unknown one is
# ignored by GitHub and fails check-codeowners.yml. `./vertra catalog validate`
# checks the layout: every team has an owner, and the admin paths below
# resolve to the same owners as the fallback.
#
# Branch protection on main must require a code owner's review, or none of
# this is enforced.

# Fallback, and the catalog admins: whoever runs this catalog. CHANGE
# @your-org/catalog-admins everywhere below to them.
* @your-org/catalog-admins

# Teams: each team's owners approve its products. Adding a team
# adds a line here, which (.github/ below) catalog admins approve:
#   /teams/<team>/ @<org>/<github-team>

# Catalog admins only. What CI runs and publishes with, the starters every
# team copies, and SecretStores (applying one changes the cluster: a team
# proposes, admins merge).
/.github/ @your-org/catalog-admins
/tools/ @your-org/catalog-admins
/vertra.yaml @your-org/catalog-admins
/vertra @your-org/catalog-admins
/templates/ @your-org/catalog-admins
/teams/*/secret-stores/ @your-org/catalog-admins
